# The guides moved into the wiki. These are the only rules in this file.
#
# Every target lives under /wiki/, and no pattern below matches its own target, which is the
# trap that made an earlier version of this file useless: it held
#     /play/*  /play/index.html  200
# and `/play/index.html` itself matches `/play/*`, so it was an infinite loop. Cloudflare
# reported "Parsed 0 valid redirect rules" and ignored THE WHOLE FILE — one bad rule takes every
# other rule with it. Keep the paths exact and keep the targets out of the patterns.
#
# /play/ needs no rule: the web game does no path-based routing (it only uses
# history.replaceState to strip ?magic= from the query string), so there are no /play/<route>
# URLs to rewrite, and /play/ resolves as an ordinary directory index.
#
# public/<name>/index.html still holds a matching stub page for each of these. That is not
# redundant: this file is Cloudflare-only, and a local desktop install serves public/ at ITS
# root, where these rules do not exist. The stubs are what answer there.
#
# /pax-historia-alternative/ deliberately has NO rule. It is a keyword-targeted landing page
# rather than wiki content, and its exact-match path is doing search work; it keeps its URL.

/guides/         /wiki/                  301
/guides          /wiki/                  301
/get-started/    /wiki/install/          301
/get-started     /wiki/install/          301
/how-to-play/    /wiki/how-to-play/      301
/how-to-play     /wiki/how-to-play/      301
